  "question": {
    "text": "Each side of a square subtends an angle of <math><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math> at the top of a tower <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;meters high standing at the center of the square. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;meters is the length of each side of the square, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> is equal to ( use&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.41</mo></math>)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "7.05",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0035_a62097d6b366.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 252px;\" /></p><p>Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> be a square with each side of length <math><mi>a</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>It is given that <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∠</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math><br />Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>M</mi></math> be the midpoint of <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∠</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∠</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></math></p><p>In <math><mo>∆</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo></math> right angled at <math><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo></math><br />we have,&nbsp;<math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∠</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />In <math><mo>∆</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> = <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>m</mi></math></p>"
  }
}